# Beszel + Traefik + Let's Encrypt — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in each value before `docker compose up`.
# `.env` is gitignored — never commit real credential values.
#
# Image versions are NOT set here. The tested tag + sha256 digest for every
# image lives in the compose file's `x-images` block, so `git pull` delivers
# the version combination this repository has tested. To pin a different
# version yourself, uncomment and set:
# BESZEL_IMAGE_TAG=henrygd/beszel:0.19.0@sha256:…

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Traefik reverse proxy
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Email address for Let's Encrypt renewal notices. REQUIRED.
TRAEFIK_ACME_EMAIL=admin@example.com

# Hostname for the Traefik dashboard (basic-auth protected). REQUIRED.
TRAEFIK_HOSTNAME=traefik.beszel.example.com

# Basic Authentication for the Traefik dashboard.
# Format: USERNAME:BCRYPT_HASH (with $ characters doubled to $$ for compose)
#     htpasswd -nbB traefikadmin YOUR_STRONG_PASSWORD | sed 's/\$/\$\$/g'
# REQUIRED — do not ship production without changing this.
TRAEFIK_BASIC_AUTH=change_me_generate_with_htpasswd_and_replace_this_string

# Log level: DEBUG, INFO, WARN, ERROR. Default: WARN.
# TRAEFIK_LOG_LEVEL=WARN

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Beszel hub
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Public hostname. Must resolve to this server's public IP for the
# Let's Encrypt TLS-ALPN challenge. REQUIRED.
#
# Beszel builds alert links AND the agent installation snippets it shows in its
# own interface from this. Wrong here and the "copy this compose" button hands
# you a broken HUB_URL — a confusing thing to debug, because everything else
# works.
BESZEL_HOSTNAME=status.example.com

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The agent's credentials — EMPTY ON PURPOSE, AND IT WILL CRASH-LOOP UNTIL SET
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Both values are issued by the hub, so they cannot exist before the hub has
# run once. The first `up -d` therefore starts an agent that restarts every few
# seconds saying "no key provided". That is the expected first state, not a
# broken configuration — CI asserts that this exact message is the one you get,
# so that a genuinely broken agent cannot hide behind it.
#
# The sequence:
#   1. docker compose … up -d
#   2. Open https://<BESZEL_HOSTNAME>, create your account
#   3. Add System. Name it, and for Host paste:  /beszel_socket/beszel.sock
#   4. Copy the key and the token it shows you into the two lines below
#   5. docker compose … up -d        (again)
#
# Step 3 is the one that looks wrong and is not: the hub reaches the agent over
# a unix socket in a shared volume rather than over the network. It has to —
# the agent runs with host networking and the hub does not, so neither can see
# the other's loopback and no Docker DNS name resolves for both.
BESZEL_AGENT_KEY=
BESZEL_AGENT_TOKEN=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The agent
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Which filesystem the root disk chart follows. Leave empty and the agent picks
# the one carrying /. Set it and it must be the name as it appears in
# /proc/diskstats — `dm-0` on LVM, not the /dev/mapper path, and `md0` for a
# software array — or you get a usage chart with permanently empty I/O.
#
#   lsblk
#   cat /proc/diskstats
# BESZEL_FILESYSTEM=

# The loopback port the socket proxy is published on, for the agent to reach.
# Published on 127.0.0.1 only; change it if something else has the port.
# BESZEL_DOCKERPROXY_PORT=2375

# Only read with disk-smart.override.yml: a device to keep out of the S.M.A.R.T.
# panel. See that file — a software array is the usual reason, and it explains
# what you give up.
# BESZEL_EXCLUDE_SMART=/dev/md0

# Timezone for timestamps and schedules.
# BESZEL_TZ=Etc/UTC

# How long Traefik holds a request or response open. The dashboard keeps
# long-lived connections for its live charts.
# BESZEL_READ_TIMEOUT=0s
# BESZEL_WRITE_TIMEOUT=0s
# BESZEL_IDLE_TIMEOUT=600s

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backups (defaults shown; override only to tune)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The archive covers the hub's data directory: the systems, the alert rules,
# the users, and every metric it has recorded. The history rides along and
# nobody restores a CPU graph from March; the alert rules are the part that is
# genuinely irreplaceable.
#
# The agent's own directory is NOT archived. It is local state, rebuilt on
# start.

# BACKUP_INIT_SLEEP=30m
# BACKUP_INTERVAL=24h
# DATA_BACKUP_PRUNE_DAYS=7
# DATA_BACKUPS_PATH=/srv/beszel-data/backups
# DATA_PATH=/beszel_data
# DATA_BACKUP_NAME=beszel-data-backup

# Resource limits (defaults shown).
# BESZEL_MEMORY_LIMIT=512m
# BESZEL_CPU_LIMIT=1.0
# BESZEL_MEMORY_RESERVATION=64m
# BESZEL_CPU_RESERVATION=0.1
# BESZEL_AGENT_MEMORY_LIMIT=256m
# BESZEL_AGENT_CPU_LIMIT=0.5
# BESZEL_AGENT_MEMORY_RESERVATION=32m
# BESZEL_AGENT_CPU_RESERVATION=0.1
# BESZEL_DOCKERPROXY_MEMORY_LIMIT=64m
# BESZEL_DOCKERPROXY_CPU_LIMIT=0.5
# BESZEL_DOCKERPROXY_MEMORY_RESERVATION=16m
# BESZEL_DOCKERPROXY_CPU_RESERVATION=0.1
# TRAEFIK_MEMORY_LIMIT=256m
# TRAEFIK_CPU_LIMIT=0.5
# TRAEFIK_MEMORY_RESERVATION=64m
# TRAEFIK_CPU_RESERVATION=0.1
# BESZEL_BACKUPS_MEMORY_LIMIT=256m
# BESZEL_BACKUPS_CPU_LIMIT=0.5
# BESZEL_BACKUPS_MEMORY_RESERVATION=16m
# BESZEL_BACKUPS_CPU_RESERVATION=0.1

# How long docker waits before SIGKILL. The hub holds a SQLite database.
# BESZEL_STOP_GRACE_PERIOD=60s

# Image versions. Every image is pinned by digest inside the compose file
# (x-images block); set the matching variable here to run a different version
# of that one image while every other pin stays as tested. Needs Docker
# Compose v2.5 or newer (2022).
#
# Note the agent: the -alpine suffix is not cosmetic. The default agent image
# is built FROM scratch and has no smartctl, so S.M.A.R.T. silently monitors
# nothing at all.
# TRAEFIK_IMAGE_VERSION=3.7
# BESZEL_IMAGE_VERSION=0.19.0
# BESZEL_AGENT_IMAGE_VERSION=0.19.0-alpine
# BESZEL_DOCKERPROXY_IMAGE_VERSION=v0.5.0
# BESZEL_BACKUPS_IMAGE_VERSION=3.22
